1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,436
One child.

2
00:00:01,716 --> 00:00:02,621
One gene.

3
00:00:02,901 --> 00:00:06,306
Mosaic variegated aneuploidy is an ultra-rare disease:

4
00:00:06,306 --> 00:00:10,529
children grow very slowly and face a high risk of childhood cancer.

5
00:00:10,809 --> 00:00:15,860
The child in this challenge, PROBAND01, carries two faulty copies of BUB1B,

6
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:18,216
the cause we pinpointed in Track 1.

7
00:00:18,866 --> 00:00:19,906
BUB1B makes BUBR1,

8
00:00:19,906 --> 00:00:24,468
a key part of the checkpoint that holds cell division until every chromosome is

9
00:00:24,468 --> 00:00:25,507
properly attached.

10
00:00:25,787 --> 00:00:29,392
One copy is cut short; the other is predicted to misfold,

11
00:00:29,392 --> 00:00:31,732
so some working BUBR1 is likely left.

12
00:00:32,012 --> 00:00:34,984
Too little of it causes two problems from one defect.

13
00:00:35,264 --> 00:00:38,909
Chromosomes are gained and lost, which raises the risk of cancer.

14
00:00:39,189 --> 00:00:43,566
And cells age too early, which is linked to growth failure and muscle loss.

15
00:00:43,846 --> 00:00:44,379
In fact,

16
00:00:44,379 --> 00:00:49,642
the first proof that clearing aged cells delays age-related disease was made in

17
00:00:49,642 --> 00:00:50,975
mice with low BubR1.

18
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:53,680
Can a drug fix the gene itself?

19
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:54,575
No.

20
00:00:54,855 --> 00:00:59,290
BUB1B is essential for every dividing cell, and no drug targets it.

21
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:04,175
The only drugs that act nearby are chemotherapies that would weaken the checkpoint

22
00:01:04,175 --> 00:01:04,737
even more.

23
00:01:05,017 --> 00:01:07,617
So we looked downstream, at the two consequences.

24
00:01:08,267 --> 00:01:12,486
We scored every candidate against eleven independent lines of evidence,

25
00:01:12,486 --> 00:01:17,062
from network medicine to real BubR1 mouse data and clinical-trial registries,

26
00:01:17,062 --> 00:01:19,320
and kept the ones most lines agree on.

27
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:23,002
A script re-checks every number in the report against its source.

28
00:01:23,652 --> 00:01:27,312
Three candidates rise to the top, ranked by evidence in children:

29
00:01:27,312 --> 00:01:30,409
one approved drug and two widely available supplements.

30
00:01:30,689 --> 00:01:32,244
First, metformin.

31
00:01:32,524 --> 00:01:37,232
It activates an energy-stress pathway that aneuploid cells tolerate poorly,

32
00:01:37,232 --> 00:01:42,066
and a trial in Fanconi anemia, another childhood genome-instability syndrome,

33
00:01:42,066 --> 00:01:45,330
gives a tested pediatric dose and reassuring safety.

34
00:01:45,610 --> 00:01:49,523
Second, nicotinamide riboside, a form of vitamin B3.

35
00:01:49,803 --> 00:01:52,505
In mice, raising NAD lifts BUBR1 levels,

36
00:01:52,505 --> 00:01:56,896
and in children with ataxia-telangiectasia it was well tolerated.

37
00:01:57,176 --> 00:02:00,416
Third, fisetin, which clears aged cells.

38
00:02:00,696 --> 00:02:05,920
It fits the aging axis best, but it has only adult data, so it comes last.

39
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:09,654
This child's pharmacogenes show no barrier to these drugs,

40
00:02:09,654 --> 00:02:12,526
though kidney function must be watched with metformin.

41
00:02:12,806 --> 00:02:16,542
And none of this replaces the recommended step: tumor surveillance,

42
00:02:16,542 --> 00:02:19,888
with a kidney ultrasound every three months until age seven.

43
00:02:20,168 --> 00:02:23,497
This is a hypothesis for a supervised single-patient trial,

44
00:02:23,497 --> 00:02:25,811
with biomarkers to tell whether it works.

45
00:02:26,091 --> 00:02:27,588
It is not a proven treatment.

46
00:02:28,238 --> 00:02:31,790
The whole pipeline uses public databases and runs on a laptop,

47
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:35,169
so it can be reused for the next child with a rare disease.

48
00:02:35,449 --> 00:02:38,712
Thank you to the child and family behind PROBAND01.

